{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts","id":910099,"title":"Homebrewed Incepts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-08T08:24:54-07:00","id":910099,"title":"Homebrewed Incepts","content":"Hey all, how are all of you? As you all know, I am a firm believer in making angels as formidable as possible.. so during work last night I had angels on the brain, and came up with a Incept that I really enjoyed, so I thought I'd share it with you today, and would ask if any of you have also made any custom Incepts to supplement the ( admittedly small number of) existing ones.<br /> <br /> It should be noted right away that going into this Incepts I had decided to make it as potent as possible in order to capture their status as Root-Access codes granted by a God, while still trying to be somewhat fair to demons or other potential enemies. It is stated that Exploits are naught but crude shadows of Incepts and as a result they should be pretty damn powerful. Sadly while canon Incepts are undeniably strong, they are not quite as good as the devs hyped them up to be - certainly not powerful or blatant enough to warrant the risk of Falling unless used in the most egregious manner possible. So I wanted to make Incepts that were a bit more frightening, the kinds of occult tools that if used by an angel during a confrontation could utterly shift the balance of power to their favor during the engagement.<br /> <br /> Without further ado, enjoy!<br /> ______<br /> <br /> <b>Galvanize</b><br /> <br /> Once activated Galvanize allows the angel to spend Essence to generate a number of temporary ( &quot;Galvanized&quot;) points of Corpus equal to Rank + 1 for the remainder of the scene( Exampiel 1.0 would gain a meager two points of temporary Corpus, Exampiel 3.0 would gain four, and Exampiel 5.0 would gain six.). Should the angel suffer damage from attack these temporary Corpus points are lost first; acting as a form of ablative shielding against damage of all types - damage inflicted by an angel's Bane bypasses the protection offered by Galvanize, however. In addition, Galvanize may be utilized multiple times per scene with an expenditure of Essence, and the angel in question may spend as many points of Essence their Rank allows each turn for the purpose of reinforcing their spiritual body with this protective &quot;layer&quot; ( Exampiel 3.0 has activated Galvanize earlier during a confrontation with a skilled Ring of Unchained, and over the course of the fight utilizes the Incept again just before the last of her Galvanized Corpus is burned away, spending all three points of Essence in order to gain twelve additional points of temporary corpus levels).<br /> <br /> The secondary effect of Galvanize allows the angel to add their Rank+1 to their Resistance Score in order to resist supernatural powers more effectively, and by spending an additional point of Willpower after activation may bestow another being with Galvanized Corpus points, though these temporary health/corpus levels cannot be additionally reinforced with replacements until the initially bestowed points expire or are expended.<br /> <br /> ________<br /> <br /> Well there you are! As always your comments are welcomed, and I would love to hear of any homebrewed Incepts you guys have come up with!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 06-08-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:01:07-07:00","id":910114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts#post910099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Galvanize</b><br /> <br /> Once activated Galvanize allows the angel to spend Essence to generate a number of temporary ( &quot;Galvanized&quot;) points of Corpus equal to Rank + 1 for the remainder of the scene( Exampiel 1.0 would gain a meager two points of temporary Corpus, Exampiel 3.0 would gain four, and Exampiel 5.0 would gain six.). Should the angel suffer damage from attack these temporary Corpus points are lost first; acting as a form of ablative shielding against damage of all types - damage inflicted by an angel's Bane bypasses the protection offered by Galvanize, however. In addition, Galvanize may be utilized multiple times per scene with an expenditure of Essence, and the angel in question may spend as many points of Essence their Rank allows each turn for the purpose of reinforcing their spiritual body with this protective &quot;layer&quot; ( Exampiel 3.0 has activated Galvanize earlier during a confrontation with a skilled Ring of Unchained, and over the course of the fight utilizes the Incept again just before the last of her Galvanized Corpus is burned away, spending all three points of Essence in order to gain twelve additional points of temporary corpus levels).<br /> <br /> The secondary effect of Galvanize allows the angel to add their Rank+1 to their Resistance Score in order to resist supernatural powers more effectively, and by spending an additional point of Willpower after activation may bestow another being with Galvanized Corpus points, though these temporary health/corpus levels cannot be additionally reinforced with replacements until the initially bestowed points expire or are expended.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does this integrate with the existing ability of Ephemerals to spend Essence to boost their Attributes by Rank + 2 for a Scene? Say Exampiel 3.0 spends 5 Essence to increase their Resistance, thus increasing their Health/Corpus by 5?<br /> <br /> This is very protection/armor focused. No use for the other meaning of Galvanize: to spur or excite something into action?<br /> <hr /><br /> I've wanted a kind of &quot;temporarily increase Influence/Effective Rank&quot; power, and I wonder if that would work as an Incept. Basic idea is that it would allow an Angel to ramp up the Influence rating of another Angel (or Spirit, or Ghost...) to enable even weaker ones access to the higher Influence effects (yes, Exampiel 5.0 doesn't have Influence: Fire, but the low Rank Angel Burniel, does... so Exampiel uses [?] to boost Burniel's Influence: Fire up so that it can create a permanent blaze necessary for Exampiel's mission/project).<br /> <hr /><br /> Another idea: A Legion like effect where the Angel actual exists as multiple semi-independent bodies. Not sure if that has been covered already.<br /> <br /> Mechanic: Maybe Angel can split into X copies with 1 Rank lower. If said copies keep the hypothetical Incept, <i>those</i> copies can also split, and so on, until there is a &quot;legion&quot; of Rank 1 Angels (which can always &quot;reintegrate&quot; up into the original). Might also serve as an Ultron/Host(from Werewolf) survival mechanism, in that even 1 copy can eventual restore into the original.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-08-2016, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T09:46:04-07:00","id":910139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=910114#post910114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How does this integrate with the existing ability of Ephemerals to spend Essence to boost their Attributes by Rank + 2 for a Scene? Say Exampiel 3.0 spends 5 Essence to increase their Resistance, thus increasing their Health/Corpus by 5?<br /> <br /> This is very protection/armor focused. No use for the other meaning of Galvanize: to spur or excite something into action? <hr /><br /> I've wanted a kind of &quot;temporarily increase Influence/Effective Rank&quot; power, and I wonder if that would work as an Incept. Basic idea is that it would allow an Angel to ramp up the Influence rating of another Angel (or Spirit, or Ghost...) to enable even weaker ones access to the higher Influence effects (yes, Exampiel 5.0 doesn't have Influence: Fire, but the low Rank Angel Burniel, does... so Exampiel uses [?] to boost Burniel's Influence: Fire up so that it can create a permanent blaze necessary for Exampiel's mission/project). <hr /><br /> Another idea: A Legion like effect where the Angel actual exists as multiple semi-independent bodies. Not sure if that has been covered already.<br /> <br /> Mechanic: Maybe Angel can split into X copies with 1 Rank lower. If said copies keep the hypothetical Incept, <i>those</i> copies can also split, and so on, until there is a &quot;legion&quot; of Rank 1 Angels (which can always &quot;reintegrate&quot; up into the original). Might also serve as an Ultron/Host(from Werewolf) survival mechanism, in that even 1 copy can eventual restore into the original.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Good question, though one I didn't think to address due to me thinking that it's only logical that their base Corpus level would increase also. It basically supplements this as a passive ability that takes effect in tandem with the primary ability, with no cost to boot aside from the initial Willpower cost, ensuring that even if an enemy eats through the Galvanized Corpus, the angel is still a bit tougher than it is normally.<br /> <br /> 2. What, being potentially indestructible against anything that isn't one's bane isn't enough for you? XD More seriously, Galvanization in a material sense is a protective covering, I didn't feel that Galvanize needed an effect that could inspire or embolden others, there are other Incepts and Numina that can do similar things. I based this on the sheer resilience of Terminators, and how no matter how superficially mangled they get, they just keep coming, as if no damage as inflicted at all. I see this as a very Guardian held Incept.. or a Destroyer. Combining this with the normal difficulty in harming an angel and holy shit is it time to start breaking out ye old angelic codexes to find out how to kill it<br /> <br /> 3. I like the first one,rough as the idea is.. perhaps you can call it Amplification, or Consolidate ( oh wait, someone made a Consolidate Incept.. though it's more similar to my Galvanize). Either way, don't let that idea go; keep at it. As for the second, there does exist a few numina that do something similar, Fork coming to mind first due to it being an angelic numen.. though one that has disappeared.. which saddens me. Either way, I like it and would love to see the idea refined more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T12:26:00-07:00","id":911037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=910114#post910114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea: A Legion like effect where the Angel actual exists as multiple semi-independent bodies. Not sure if that has been covered already.<br /> <br /> Mechanic: Maybe Angel can split into X copies with 1 Rank lower. If said copies keep the hypothetical Incept, <i>those</i> copies can also split, and so on, until there is a &quot;legion&quot; of Rank 1 Angels (which can always &quot;reintegrate&quot; up into the original). Might also serve as an Ultron/Host(from Werewolf) survival mechanism, in that even 1 copy can eventual restore into the original.</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a Numen in the quickstart I haven't seen elsewhere called &quot;Fork&quot;. Spend 5 Essence, touch a reflective surface, and an exact copy of the Angel that used the Numen emerges, albeit without the Fork Numen. Pair that with the Units Incept and things could get very ugly very fast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:18:20-07:00","id":911134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=911037#post911037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There was a Numen in the quickstart I haven't seen elsewhere called &quot;Fork&quot;. Spend 5 Essence, touch a reflective surface, and an exact copy of the Angel that used the Numen emerges, albeit without the Fork Numen. Pair that with the Units Incept and things could get very ugly very fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I have an Angel who has Fork and Units- it gets ugly indeed. In fact, the players are likely to never even meet the real angel. I was always saddened that they didn't include Fork, it is a very good example of an angelic numen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T14:22:53-07:00","id":911141,"title":"","content":"With my players, it makes them absolutely terrified of this one Destroyer, because it's the one that gets sent after them if anyone has the Hunted Condition. A single Angel can quickly become a squad unto itself, which makes an already frightening Rank 3 opponent into something a lot worse.<br /> <br /> How did you handle the copies? If they are 'killed' or run out of Essence they just vanish, or would a copy be conceivably still functional?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T15:36:30-07:00","id":911196,"title":"","content":"I have them shatter and cease to exist- otherwise the cap would be hit too soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T09:14:30-07:00","id":918657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=910114#post910114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea: A Legion like effect where the Angel actual exists as multiple semi-independent bodies. Not sure if that has been covered already.<br /> <br /> Mechanic: Maybe Angel can split into X copies with 1 Rank lower. If said copies keep the hypothetical Incept, <i>those</i> copies can also split, and so on, until there is a &quot;legion&quot; of Rank 1 Angels (which can always &quot;reintegrate&quot; up into the original). Might also serve as an Ultron/Host(from Werewolf) survival mechanism, in that even 1 copy can eventual restore into the original.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rough notes so far. Probably needs better formatting and ordering.<br /> <br /> <b>Division</b><br /> <br /> Once activated, Division allows an Angel to splinter into 4 other Angels, one Rank lower, by paying 4 Essence. These Angels are constructed using the original as a baseline (using its Attribute spread, albeit at lower values, selecting Numina and Manifestations from its list, even Incepts from those it has available) with the exception of being barred from possessing the Discorporate Manifestation. The duplicates have the same original personality, mission, Ban, and Bane (though the Ban and Bane may become more generalized as Rank decreases, if the Storyteller wishes). The original's current Essence and damage are split amongst the copies at the time they are generated. If the copies are created with the Division Incept, they can even splinter themselves further, to a minimum Rank of 1. 4 copies of the same Rank can merge to return to their original Angel as an Instant action. These copies lose 1 Corpus per day. Each copy destroyed incurs 1 extra day before the original Angel can fully reincorporate. The original Angel can only be destroyed permanently if all its copied are depleted of Essence and their Corpus filled with Aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The secondary effect of Division allows damage to be split amongst willing allied beings, with at least half of the damage inflicted (to a minimum of 1) remaining with the Angel. This damage is the same type (Bashing, Lethal, Aggravated) as would be inflicted upon the Angel, and cannot be reduced by Armor, though it can be healed as normal for its type afterwards. <hr /><br /> Thoughts? For reference, a Rank 5 Angel could split into up to 256 Rank 1 shards. Each would individually be quite weak, but they <i>can</i> be a one-Angel flash mob. The ban on Discorporation is to prevent the Angel from immediately Discorporating one of their copies as &quot;insurance&quot;. This is still likely overpowered, even for Incepts, but I'm not sure what exactly to do to weaken it but still allow the exponential growth factor at higher Ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 06-22-2016, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T09:38:27-07:00","id":918667,"title":"","content":"I like it, though if they are copies, I see no point ban or banes changing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T09:51:58-07:00","id":918672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=918667#post918667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it, though if they are copies, I see no point ban or banes changing</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as ephemerals decrease in Rank, their Bans and Banes become more common. A Rank 5 might have a very specific Bane. Didn't seem right to keep any Rank 2 or 1 copies with the same obscure Bane. I'd definitely keep them in theme, though (Rank 5 - the bones of a <i>specific </i>Saint getting generalized to <i>any</i> Saint, or even <i>anyone</i> with Integrity 7+).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T10:26:15-07:00","id":918680,"title":"","content":"True, but at the same time, these are copies, they shouldn't just have different bans/banes because of rank. For example, Idigam can create offshoots of themselves that are lower rank, yet they have the same Bans and Banes as their creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T10:37:04-07:00","id":918684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=918680#post918680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, but at the same time, these are copies, they shouldn't just have different bans/banes because of rank. For example, Idigam can create offshoots of themselves that are lower rank, yet they have the same Bans and Banes as their creator.</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; Then they can be left as is. It was a narrative suggestion, as opposed to a hard rule.<br /> <br /> What about the other parts? Do I need to add a cost to use? Clarify the Split action type as Instant? Stipulate Conditions and Tilts are copied when splitting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T13:51:27-07:00","id":918789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/910099-homebrewed-incepts?p=918684#post918684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then they can be left as is. It was a narrative suggestion, as opposed to a hard rule.<br /> <br /> What about the other parts? Do I need to add a cost to use? Clarify the Split action type as Instant? Stipulate Conditions and Tilts are copied when splitting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the cost should be paid each use, and that conditions and tilts wouldnt be split due to the possibility of a copy being undamaged and all that jazz- doesn't make sense to suffer from Ar